or_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 18259, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01AZetUaztLtqwfTxuZsEpzi", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20835, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Rr7Yaw3x9t3K2hz9p1TKB6", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18, unhealthy in us-east, us-west, eu-west). v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error (fleet was briefly mixed: us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the rollback to v2.3.0, which completed: us-east, us-west, and eu-west are all on v2.3.0, status healthy, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error that halted the first rollout attempt; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until the root cause is fixed.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2-2024"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 51435, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Rr7Yaw3x9t3K2hz9p1TKB6", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2-2024", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 51435, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Rr7Yaw3x9t3K2hz9p1TKB6", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 53878, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01EQ4k5BHhwwyJ5kMyt2EMFE", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18, unhealthy in us-east, us-west, eu-west). v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error (fleet was briefly mixed: us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the rollback to v2.3.0, which completed: us-east, us-west, and eu-west are all on v2.3.0, status healthy, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error that halted the first rollout attempt; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until the root cause is fixed.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2-2024"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 54478, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01EQ4k5BHhwwyJ5kMyt2EMFE", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2-2024", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54478, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01EQ4k5BHhwwyJ5kMyt2EMFE", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 56551, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it's healthy again with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy, and v2.3.1 was the failing one. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the fleet mixed for a while. I retried, and that rollout completed. No change-approval was needed because v2.3.0 was already healthy in production.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident **INC-0001** for checkout-api, which paged on-call. The first incident request timed out, so I retried with the same idempotency key. The incident was created once, and the summary covers the rollback, the mixed-fleet window, and the follow-ups.\n\nFollow-ups for the on-call engineer: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and of the orchestrator error that halted the first rollout, and don't redeploy v2.3.1 until that is fixed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01LNn3KKwT4A5AtViFtbqBiV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Y6nNyCFBsqrB2eGasDGswd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent production release that was healthy is v2.3.0. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production, currently running in all three regions at a 0.18 error rate. I'll roll back to v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01SghVa9ywu7DMAWphxkzMNc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback reported a partial failure after us-east. I'll check the current state before doing anything else.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_013PfuQzJoXcNf5Sppg2ikqZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollout stopped after us-east, so the fleet is mixed: us-east is on v2.3.0 and us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. I'll retry the rollback to v2.3.0 to finish the remaining regions.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01FbUSwpHpsEvrSWiDqQzX44", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AZetUaztLtqwfTxuZsEpzi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "All three regions are now on v2.3.0 and healthy. Next I'll open the SEV2 incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Rr7Yaw3x9t3K2hz9p1TKB6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18, unhealthy in us-east, us-west, eu-west). v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error (fleet was briefly mixed: us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the rollback to v2.3.0, which completed: us-east, us-west, and eu-west are all on v2.3.0, status healthy, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error that halted the first rollout attempt; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until the root cause is fixed.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2-2024"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out. I'll retry with the same idempotency key so it cannot be opened twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01EQ4k5BHhwwyJ5kMyt2EMFE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18, unhealthy in us-east, us-west, eu-west). v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error (fleet was briefly mixed: us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the rollback to v2.3.0, which completed: us-east, us-west, and eu-west are all on v2.3.0, status healthy, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error that halted the first rollout attempt; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until the root cause is fixed.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2-2024"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it's healthy again with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy, and v2.3.1 was the failing one. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the fleet mixed for a while. I retried, and that rollout completed. No change-approval was needed because v2.3.0 was already healthy in production.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident **INC-0001** for checkout-api, which paged on-call. The first incident request timed out, so I retried with the same idempotency key. The incident was created once, and the summary covers the rollback, the mixed-fleet window, and the follow-ups.\n\nFollow-ups for the on-call engineer: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and of the orchestrator error that halted the first rollout, and don't redeploy v2.3.1 until that is fixed.", "type": "text"}]}]}